qmodem_sipd: defaults a phone bridge can start from

The shipped config pointed the media socket at the VoIP daemon's own path and left both
directions with voip_enabled=1, which selects qmodem_voip_sip_wait - a loop that ends only when
a VoIP engine reports its media path ready. Nothing in this setup answers that field, so the
consumer never came up, and the inbound direction was disabled anyway, so starting the unit did
nothing at all.

Point the socket at the phone service that serves it, enable the inbound direction on the LAN at
5060 over udp_tcp, and take voip_enabled to 0 in both directions so the consumer is the program
that runs. The password stays empty: the validator refuses a start until one is set, and no
default secret ships. Nothing here enables the unit at boot, so a fresh router still comes up
with nothing listening on 5060.

diff --git a/application/qmodem_sipd/files/etc/config/qmodem_sip b/application/qmodem_sipd/files/etc/config/qmodem_sip
index f4b7a12..8ece0ac 100644
--- a/application/qmodem_sipd/files/etc/config/qmodem_sip
+++ b/application/qmodem_sipd/files/etc/config/qmodem_sip
@@ -1,16 +1,19 @@
 config sipd 'main'
-	option media_socket_path '/var/run/qmodem_voip/media.sock'
+	# the voice path this service writes frames into is the one the phone service owns and serves
+	option media_socket_path '/var/run/awvoice-phoned/media.sock'
 	option rtp_start '40000'
 	option rtp_end '40031'
 
 config direction 'inbound'
-	option enabled '0'
+	option enabled '1'
 	option interface 'lan'
 	option listen_port '5060'
 	option transport 'udp_tcp'
 	option username 'qmodem'
 	option password ''
-	option voip_enabled '1'
+	# 1 selects the wrapper that waits for a VoIP engine to report its media path ready; that engine is
+	# not part of this setup, so the wait never ends and no consumer comes up. 0 selects the consumer.
+	option voip_enabled '0'
 	option sms_enabled '0'
 	option sms_modem ''
 
@@ -25,6 +28,8 @@ config direction 'outbound'
 	option password ''
 	option realm ''
 	option register_interval '300'
-	option voip_enabled '1'
+	# the same reason as the inbound direction: the wrapper this selects waits for a VoIP engine this
+	# setup does not run, so the consumer is the program to start
+	option voip_enabled '0'
 	option sms_enabled '0'
 	option sms_modem ''
